Description: <short summary of the patch>
 22:22 <twb> Can I just make a debian/patches/stfu.patch that removes the exact versions from upstream's Cargo.toml?
 22:23 <cjwatson> twb: https://rust-team.pages.debian.net/book/fix-problems.html
 22:23 <cjwatson> The Rust team has loads of "relax-deps" patches for that sort of thing
 22:28 <twb> cool
 23:28 <twb> When patching Cargo.toml dependencies, how do I say "literally any version, I don't care"?
 23:29 <twb> That seems easier than changing it to match the exact verson Debian happens to currently have
Author: Trent W. Buck <trentbuck@gmail.com>

---
The information above should follow the Patch Tagging Guidelines, please
checkout https://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/ to learn about the format. Here
are templates for supplementary fields that you might want to add:

Origin: (upstream|backport|vendor|other), (<patch-url>|commit:<commit-id>)
